{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "MyScoutee contact permission persistence",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Typed contact-permission reads and optimistic writes owned by chat. Identity-issued actor delegation binds the current participant, REAL/DEMO session mode, method, path and exact body. Native permission persistence and version checks remain in ContactPermissionService. Maximum request and single-record response: 16 KiB; user list response: 2 MiB. Save is never automatically retried: a lost reply is an unknown outcome; a read can reconcile the saved permission/version, but does not establish completion of downstream account counters or notifications. These downstream workflow guarantees require separate verification. An explicit replay of the identical immutable Change returns the existing receipt only when every field and the expected next version match. Different payloads and later transitions retain optimistic conflicts. Accounts persists the accepted change before calling and separately resumes its account/notification effects; the transport itself still makes one attempt."
  },
